  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Emergency Response for Older Men and Women and Older People with Disabilities in Mozambique affected by Cyclone Idai</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased access of older women, men and people with disabilities to age friendly health services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More Older people in the affected areas are able to log their complaints through a strengthened grievance redressal system</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Older women and men and people with disabilities of the affected population have reduced vulnerability</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds on existing HelpAge measures and ensures that vulnerable people receive the necessary support. Measures in the areas of inclusion/protection and health (including PSS) are implemented either by HelpAge/ ASADEC directly or by the outreach teams. This complements interventions already underway and meets the most urgent needs of the target group.</narrative>
  </description>
